# ZView launchable applications, read by zview at startup.
# One line per app:  name:execpath:multi:icon:X,Y   (the last two optional)
#   name        menu label, and the placeholder icon's label (multi=1 entries
#               show "New <name>" under the icon)
#   execpath    program; run with a bare argv (no window arguments)
#   multi       1 = may open many (launcher shows "New <name>...");
#               0 = single instance (launcher shows "<name>..."; re-launch raises it)
#   icon        .icn under /usr/hr/icons: puts a PLACEHOLDER icon on the desktop
#               at start-up.  It looks like a minimised app minus the corner
#               badge (that marks a live process), and NO process exists
#               behind it -- clicking it launches the program,
#               which is what replaced starting every app resident with -H from
#               the rc script (a whole process held in memory per icon).  A
#               single-instance entry's placeholder leaves the desktop while its
#               window is open and returns when it closes; a multi entry's stays
#               put, and every click starts a fresh copy.
#   X,Y         where a placeholder launch puts the window (top-left of the
#               frame); left out, the window opens at the click.
#
# The window itself -- title, size, icon while ACTUALLY minimised, whether it
# may be stretched -- is NOT configured here: the application declares it at
# start-up (hr_open, see inc/hrapp.h), so a program can also be run straight
# from a shell.  The icon named here exists only for the placeholder, which is
# on screen before the program is; once the app runs, its own declaration wins.
#
# The rc script /usr/hr/etc/rc still runs at desktop start-up, for anything
# that should be genuinely RESIDENT from power-on.
Shell:/usr/hr/bin/zterm:1:term.icn:48,88
Files:/usr/hr/bin/zfile:1:file.icn:120,100
Editor:/usr/hr/bin/zedit:1:edit.icn:80,60
Mail:/usr/hr/bin/zmail:0:mail.icn:100,120
Manual:/usr/hr/bin/zman:0:man.icn:180,140
Calculator:/usr/hr/bin/zcalc:0:calc.icn:600,180
Printer:/usr/hr/bin/zprint:0:printer.icn:380,300
Monitor:/usr/hr/bin/zmon:0:monitor.icn:300,180
Puzzle:/usr/hr/bin/zpuzzle:0:puzzle.icn:700,300
Clock:/usr/hr/bin/zclock:0:clock.icn:720,88
